<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea in dollar repo pact with China bank.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea in dollar repo pact with China bank.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's central Bank of Korea (BOK) signed on Friday a dollar repurchase agreement (repo) with the People's Bank of China, a BOK statement said.</p>
<p>The agreement would provide the central banks with standby liquidity that could be tapped in case of a temporary but massive withdrawal of foreign currency.</p>
<p>The statement said the agreement would allow participating central banks to raise needed foreign hard currency by using their U.S. Treasury holdings to guarantee a promise to buy the same amount at a specific date. The banks would not need to liquidate their securities holdings.</p>
</text>
